{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MZqkfJfUtTKJNT2w2JfLbF","type":"tool_result","content":"== candidate_3_repair_1\nagent.jsonl\nATTEMPT_NOTE.md\nCANDIDATE_BRIEF.md\ncandidate.py\nCONTEXT.md\ncritiques.md\nexisting_hypotheses.md\nhypothesis.md\nmodel_name.txt\nrefinement_menu.md\nscratch\nRefinement of the incumbent `personal_lapse_ideal_alternation`: people still judge a sequence as more random the closer its proportion of alternations lies to their own personal ideal switching rate, and still guess on some trials at a personal, trait-like lapse rate, but when they do engage the comparison they also notice the single longest streak of identical flips and treat a longer streak as a sign of non-randomness beyond what the overall alternation rate shows. The one change is this shared longest-streak penalty inside the engaged decision (taken from `ideal_alternation_streak_penalty`), because the critique shows that among pairs matched on alternation rate people pick the sequence with the shorter longest run more often than the incumbent predicts.\nlapse_ideal_alternation_streak_aversion\n== candidate_5_repair_1\nagent.jsonl\nATTEMPT_NOTE.md\nCANDIDATE_BRIEF.md\ncandidate.py\nCONTEXT.md\ncritiques.md\nexisting_hypotheses.md\nhypothesis.md\nmodel_name.txt\nrefinement_menu.md\nscratch\nRefinement of `ideal_alternation_streak_penalty`: each person judges a sequence as more random the closer its proportion of alternations lies to their own personal ideal switching rate, and everyone additionally treats a long longest streak of identical flips as a sign of non-randomness beyond what the alternation rate shows. The one change is grafting in the incumbent's decision rule: on some trials a person does not compare the sequences and guesses, at a personal lapse rate drawn from a population, so the streak and alternation preferences are no longer diluted by trying to fit indifferent participants with one shared sensitivity — addressing the cri